(test_uuid,'Listening · Classroom Practice','choice','Why does the student speak with the librarian?',null,'Listen to a conversation between a student and a librarian. Student: Hi, I’m trying to reserve a study room for my project group tomorrow evening, but the online system says everything is full. Librarian: How many people are in your group? Student: Five. We can meet any time after six. Librarian: Reservations sometimes get cancelled late in the day. Check the system again after six tonight. If nothing opens, the media room is available from seven to eight-thirty. It seats up to eight people, but you need to complete this short request form. Student: That could work. Does the room have a screen? Librarian: Yes, and a cable for a laptop. Student: Great. I’ll fill out the form now, just in case.','["To pay a late fee", "To reserve a study room", "To replace an identification card", "To request a new textbook"]'::jsonb,'"To reserve a study room"'::jsonb,null,'published'::public.content_status,31,'original','User-supplied TOEFL iBT 2026–Aligned Classroom Mock Form A; README declares all items original and not official ETS items.',now()),
